  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Filippo Biondi, a scientist who uses satellite radar to scan beneath the pyramids, tells podcast host Jesse Michels about his project on Khafre, the second great pyramid at Giza in Egypt. He says that for this work his team used a low incidence angle, meaning the radar looked at the ground from a shallow slant. It is part of the method he says revealed structures deep under the pyramid, which, if real, would point to a hidden underground world at Giza."
